            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical study of the low dose oral contraceptive novynette].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors review the efficacy, control of the menstrual cycle and the tolerance of the low-dosed oral contraceptive Novynette (20 mkg EE/150 desogestrel) of Gedeon Richter at 25 women, included in the study. The results show: Pearl index = 0.00, a good control over the menstrual cycle, not significant and transitor side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
